1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,695
You see color with three types of receptors.

2
00:00:02,695 --> 00:00:04,256
A mantis shrimp has twelve.

3
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:05,000
It sees ultraviolet.

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,561
And it was the first animal ever shown to see circularly polarized light.

5
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:16,127
Each eye sits on its own stalk, moves on its own, and can judge depth by itself.

6
00:00:16,617 --> 00:00:19,049
So you'd see colors no human ever has?

7
00:00:19,049 --> 00:00:19,689
Not quite.

8
00:00:19,689 --> 00:00:23,913
In tests, they were worse than us at telling similar colors apart.

9
00:00:23,913 --> 00:00:26,729
We can spot differences of a few nanometers.

10
00:00:26,729 --> 00:00:29,417
They often failed below about twenty-five.

11
00:00:29,917 --> 00:00:34,702
Scientists think they recognize colors instantly instead of comparing them.

12
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:35,850
Speed over detail.

13
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:39,806
Handy, when your punch moves at over twenty meters per second.

14
00:00:40,317 --> 00:00:42,230
What if your skin could eat sunlight?

15
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,574
Full story on the channel.
